  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115680",
      "title": "Component Cleanup with ngOnDestroy",
      "lectureOrder": 126,
      "videoOrder": 120,
      "sourceHash": "24f6d12e127a9905ef57e02178dffd235fdc739d6ba97432a1e62e06792ef1b2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 4.71,
          "en": "So now that we had a thorough first look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.71,
          "end": 6.6,
          "en": "at all these lifecycle hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.6,
          "end": 10.47,
          "en": "and these methods you can add to your Angular components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.47,
          "end": 12.84,
          "en": "we'll move back to the main project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.84,
          "end": 15.51,
          "en": "Though you'll see some of these hooks in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.51,
          "end": 18.48,
          "en": "throughout this course, and also later in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.48,
          "end": 21.18,
          "en": "I'll also get back to afterNextRender",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.18,
          "end": 22.653,
          "en": "and afterRender later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.76,
          "end": 26.01,
          "en": "But one hook I actually want to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.01,
          "end": 29.64,
          "en": "to our main project right away, right now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.64,
          "end": 31.86,
          "en": "is the ngOnDestroy hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.86,
          "end": 36.09,
          "en": "because we got a use case for that in our project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.09,
          "end": 38.52,
          "en": "Now to make sure I don't have any typos,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.52,
          "end": 42.72,
          "en": "I'll implement OnInit and OnDestroy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.72,
          "end": 44.343,
          "en": "separated by a comma,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.3,
          "end": 49.533,
          "en": "and OnDestroy must be imported from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.67,
          "end": 51.81,
          "en": "And with it imported,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.81,
          "end": 55.86,
          "en": "I then have to add the ngOnDestroy method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.86,
          "end": 58.98,
          "en": "By the way, the order of the methods does not matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.98,
          "end": 60.483,
          "en": "The order is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.22,
          "end": 64.23,
          "en": "But now, here, in ngOnDestroy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.23,
          "end": 66.39,
          "en": "we can do cleanup work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.39,
          "end": 67.95,
          "en": "We might want to perform",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.95,
          "end": 72.33,
          "en": "right before the component is gone, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.33,
          "end": 73.83,
          "en": "Now here in my application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.83,
          "end": 76.41,
          "en": "this component is actually never gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.41,
          "end": 78.48,
          "en": "We can't switch to other pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.48,
          "end": 80.64,
          "en": "and we're not rendering it conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.64,
          "end": 82.143,
          "en": "So it's always there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.07,
          "end": 85.38,
          "en": "But for some components, that might be different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.38,
          "end": 87.9,
          "en": "And since I'm setting up an interval here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.9,
          "end": 89.7,
          "en": "and we might, in the future,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 89.7,
          "end": 93,
          "en": "use this component such that it may disappear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 93,
          "end": 95.31,
          "en": "it is a good idea to clean up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 95.31,
          "end": 98.7,
          "en": "that interval whenever that component is removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.7,
          "end": 101.22,
          "en": "Because even though if that's not the case yet here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.22,
          "end": 102.50999999999999,
          "en": "in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.50999999999999,
          "end": 104.55,
          "en": "that might change in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.55,
          "end": 106.41,
          "en": "And if you have an interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106.41,
          "end": 108.75,
          "en": "that keeps on going behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 108.75,
          "end": 110.75999999999999,
          "en": "even though the component is gone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 110.75999999999999,
          "end": 113.7,
          "en": "you have a memory leak in your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 113.7,
          "end": 116.7,
          "en": "and you can have a negative impact on the performance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 116.7,
          "end": 118.2,
          "en": "of your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 118.2,
          "end": 120.453,
          "en": "which no one wants, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 122.61,
          "end": 126.36,
          "en": "That's why we should clean up our interval here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 126.36,
          "end": 128.013,
          "en": "with ngOnDestroy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 128.85,
          "end": 130.44,
          "en": "Now how can we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 130.44,
          "end": 135.44,
          "en": "Well, setInterval returns a value of type NodeJS.Timeout,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 136.29,
          "end": 138.06,
          "en": "which is basically an ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 138.06,
          "end": 140.133,
          "en": "of the interval that's created here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 141.32999999999998,
          "end": 144.24,
          "en": "So we can add a new private property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 144.24,
          "end": 146.46,
          "en": "private since we don't need it in the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 146.46,
          "end": 148.053,
          "en": "and name it interval.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 149.28,
          "end": 153.24,
          "en": "And the type should be NodeJS.Timeout,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 153.24,
          "end": 156.483,
          "en": "or undefined, so I'll add this question mark here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 159.15,
          "end": 161.94,
          "en": "And then we should set this interval here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 161.94,
          "end": 165.003,
          "en": "to the result of calling setInterval.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 166.98,
          "end": 170.64,
          "en": "Now we can use it in ngOnDestroy to remove it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 170.64,
          "end": 173.553,
          "en": "with help of the clearTimeout method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.87,
          "end": 178.07999999999998,
          "en": "To that, we can pass this interval.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 178.07999999999998,
          "end": 181.773,
          "en": "So this ID, which we stored in this interval property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.72,
          "end": 185.07,
          "en": "And with that, we're making sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 185.07,
          "end": 187.26,
          "en": "that this interval gets cleaned up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 187.26,
          "end": 189.75,
          "en": "when the component is removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 189.75,
          "end": 192.84,
          "en": "Again, this component is never removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 192.84,
          "end": 195.72,
          "en": "Nonetheless, that is something you typically want to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 198.72,
          "en": "to avoid potential memory leaks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 198.72,
          "end": 200.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now you might be getting an error here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 200.57999999999998,
          "end": 203.76,
          "en": "regarding this NodeJS.Timeout thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 203.76,
          "end": 205.26,
          "en": "And if that's the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 205.26,
          "end": 209.49,
          "en": "you can replace this type with ReturnType,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 209.49,
          "end": 213.037,
          "en": "which is a special type provided by TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 213.037,
          "end": 215.257,
          "en": "<typeof setInterval.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 217.89,
          "end": 221.1,
          "en": "Now that's a bit more advanced TypeScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 221.1,
          "end": 223.2,
          "en": "and it's all TypeScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 223.2,
          "end": 225.21,
          "en": "it has nothing to do with Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 225.21,
          "end": 226.11,
          "en": "which simply means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 226.11,
          "end": 228.81,
          "en": "that the type of interval should be the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 228.81,
          "end": 231.793,
          "en": "of value returned by setInterval.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 233.04,
          "end": 235.95,
          "en": "And with that, this error should go away,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 235.95,
          "end": 238.68,
          "en": "and the application should work as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 238.68,
          "end": 242.16,
          "en": "But now, the interval is theoretically removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 242.16,
          "end": 245.403,
          "en": "when that component is removed from the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
